## Problem

In [`batch_queue.rs:388-390`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/48b31f0b1b1e9afcf4d07f75c28771f602cc6a1b/rust/kona/crates/protocol/derive/src/stages/batch/batch_queue.rs#L388-L390), when `get_singular_batches` fails on a span batch, it returns a `Critical` error:

```rust
let batches = match sb.get_singular_batches(&self.l1_blocks, parent).map_err(|e| {
    PipelineError::BadEncoding(PipelineEncodingError::SpanBatchError(e)).crit() // ← wrong
}) {
```

`get_singular_batches` can fail with `SpanBatchError` variants that are triggered by **bad external data** from the batcher:
- `TooBigSpanBatchSize`, `BitfieldTooLong`, `EmptySpanBatch`
- Decoding errors: `InvalidTransactionData`, `RelativeTimestamp`, etc.

## Why it matters

A `Critical` error halts derivation entirely. A malicious or buggy batcher can craft a span batch that passes channel-level validation but fails at singular batch extraction, halting the node.

The post-Holocene equivalent [`batch_stream.rs:199-205`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/48b31f0b1b1e9afcf4d07f75c28771f602cc6a1b/rust/kona/crates/protocol/derive/src/stages/batch/batch_stream.rs#L199-L205) correctly handles this by flushing and returning `NotEnoughData.temp()`:

```rust
Err(e) => {
    warn!(target: "batch_span", "Extracting singular batches from span batch failed: {}", e);
    self.flush();
    Err(PipelineError::NotEnoughData.temp())
}
```

## Fix

```rust
let batches = match sb.get_singular_batches(&self.l1_blocks, parent) {
    Ok(b) => b,
    Err(e) => {
        warn!(target: "batch_queue", "Failed to extract singular batches from span batch, flushing: {}", e);
        self.prev.flush();
        return Err(PipelineError::NotEnoughData.temp());
    }
};
```

